      "message": "Regarding the AIDL v1 allocator path (lines 1094–1104):\n`status.getExceptionCode()` and `status.getServiceSpecificError()` return positive integer values (`AllocationError::BAD_DESCRIPTOR \u003d 1`, `AllocationError::NO_RESOURCES \u003d 2`, etc.), leaving the AIDL allocation path vulnerable to the exact same positive status_t return code issue.\n\nEven though mentioned in the commit message notes, fixing the AIDL v1 path here (mapping `AllocationError` to negative `status_t` codes similarly to `Gralloc5.cpp:273-284`) would ensure all allocation paths in `Gralloc4Allocator::allocate` consistently adhere to the negative error code convention.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
