      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good fix mapping tmpError from the HIDL callback to status_t.\n\nHowever, notice line 1170 at the end of this method:\n```cpp\nreturn (ret.isOk()) ? error : static_cast\u003cstatus_t\u003e(kTransactionError);\n```\n`kTransactionError` is defined as `Error::NO_RESOURCES` (value 5). If `!ret.isOk()` (such as when the HIDL transaction fails or the allocator service dies), casting `kTransactionError` to `status_t` returns `+5`, which is positive and will still be interpreted as success by callers like `GraphicBuffer::initCheck()` and `BufferQueueProducer::dequeueBuffer()`.\n\nWe should map `kTransactionError` through `hidlErrorToStatusT(kTransactionError)` (or return `UNKNOWN_TRANSACTION` / `FAILED_TRANSACTION` / `DEAD_OBJECT`) when `!ret.isOk()` so transaction failures also return negative `status_t` error codes.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
